{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_response_cache_response_cache_middleware", "label": "Response cache middleware (page)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/response-cache.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_response_cache_cached", "label": "cached handler wrapper", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/response-cache.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A cache hit serves the stored response without invoking the underlying handler; which handlers to wrap is a per-handler decision."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_response_cache_responsecacheoptions", "label": "ResponseCacheOptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/response-cache.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_response_cache_cachestatuses", "label": "cacheStatuses", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/response-cache.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Defaults to [200] so a transient 500 never sticks around for the TTL; add 404 where many lookups miss, to save repeat database hits."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_response_cache_cache_key_composition", "label": "Cache key composition", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/response-cache.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "key(req) is the entire cache-key contract. req.path is the pathname only, so an endpoint that varies by a query parameter must fold it into the key or every page shares one entry and page 2 is served page 1."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_response_cache_stampede_protection", "label": "Per-process single-flight stampede protection", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/response-cache.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "On a miss the handler runs once per process and the other concurrent requests await that result; it is not cluster-wide, so with N pods the handler can run N times, and stale-while-revalidate is not built in."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_response_cache_cache_invalidation", "label": "Cache invalidation by TTL or manual delete", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/response-cache.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No auto-invalidation on writes: staleness is bounded by ttlMs, or you delete the prefixed key directly because the cache is just a Cache."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_response_cache_key_minting_side", "label": "The key-minting side of a shared cache", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/response-cache.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "key(request) almost always derives from client-controlled input, so a caller who varies it mints an entry per request. Harmless alone \u2014 the LRU bound is exactly what stops the response cache growing \u2014 and these plain sets are drained before a rate-limit counter, but the bound is still hard and Memcached and Redis under allkeys-lru have no such policy."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_response_cache_response_cache_middleware", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_response_cache_cached", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/response-cache.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_response_cache_cached", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_response_cache_responsecacheoptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/response-cache.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_response_cache_responsecacheoptions", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_response_cache_cachestatuses", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/response-cache.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_response_cache_cache_key_composition", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_response_cache_cached", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/response-cache.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_response_cache_stampede_protection", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_response_cache_cached", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/response-cache.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_response_cache_cache_invalidation", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_response_cache_cached", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/response-cache.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_response_cache_key_minting_side", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_response_cache_cache_key_composition", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/response-cache.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_response_cache_response_cache_middleware", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_rate_limit_ratelimit", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/response-cache.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_response_cache_key_minting_side", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_rate_limit_fixed_window_counting", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/response-cache.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_response_cache_key_minting_side", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_registry_caps", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.75, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/response-cache.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}], "hyperedges": []}